{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the chief of the butlers appointed.</b> Now when these eunuchs were placed in the house of the chief of the butlers, he appointed Joseph, and the meaning is he remembered his words and brought him to his house, and placed him in the pit, which is the prison, and this is the opinion of the great grammarian [Saadia?], and in my opinion the prison house was in the house of the chief of the butlers, and there Joseph was, and the proof is 'the place where Joseph was confined there,' and the chief of the butlers commanded that Joseph be with them to serve them, for they held high rank in the house of Pharaoh, for they were officers:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:33.020313351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}